Content shell: popups to the embedder, with their opener.

A window a page opens (window.open, a link to a new window) is made by the
shell as a window of its own, and nothing outside the shell hears of it.
zebkit's application is now told of each with the page that opened it
(zebkit_view_on_window_open()), so that it shows the popup, in a window or off
the screen, while the two stay linked: window.opener, postMessage() and
window.closed, which a site's sign-in through a popup ("Sign in with
Google", as in Firefox) relies on.

